{"title":"Cooga Georgeooga-Harryooga Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proofs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proofs</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Applications\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Applications</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Application_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Application 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-4 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Testimonials\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Testimonials</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>The Cooga Georgeooga-Harryooga Theorem (Circular Georgeooga-Harryooga Theorem) states that if you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> distinguishable objects and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> objects are kept away from each other, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42f070957b35ef866966fd336f0ce6c0cc6faf75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a-b)!^2}{(a-2b)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" /> ways to arrange the objects in a circle.\n</p><p><br />\nCreated by George and Harry of <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC50E9TuLIMWbOPUX45xZPaQ\">The Ooga Booga Tribe of The Caveman Society</a>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proofs\">Proofs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proofs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_1\">Proof 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let our group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> objects be represented like so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, ..., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6873715a60ff7706da71b8cad30cead78b1ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Let the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> objects be the ones we can't have together.\n</p><p>Then we can organize our objects like so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/e/bded4c8eb437eac7c96ffdda3c7f36dc774fb40c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] label(&quot;$1$&quot;, dir(90)); label(&quot;BLANK&quot;, dir(60)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, dir(30)); label(&quot;BLANK&quot;, dir(0)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, dir(-30)); label(&quot;BLANK&quot;, dir(-60)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, dir(-90)); label(&quot;BLANK&quot;, dir(-120)); label(&quot;$a-b-1$&quot;, dir(-150)); label(&quot;BLANK&quot;, dir(-180)); label(&quot;$a-b$&quot;, dir(-210)); label(&quot;BLANK&quot;, dir(-240)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb5ae6ac1eadc478af8a04652a4357b869baf0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> ways to arrange the objects in that list.\n</p><p>Now we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a697bfdeadf2105048670e6f6c7d4dc6878dc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> blanks and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> other objects so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/14338f3a9796b753a82392b13b35333a29751567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$_{a-b}P_{b}=\\frac{(a-b)!}{(a-2b)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"137\" height=\"43\" /> ways to arrange the objects we can't put together.\n</p><p>By The Fundamental Counting Principal our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42f070957b35ef866966fd336f0ce6c0cc6faf75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a-b)!^2}{(a-2b)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nProof by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:RedFireTruck&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:RedFireTruck (page does not exist)\"><font color=\"#FF0000\">RedFireTruck</font></a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:RedFireTruck\" title=\"User talk:RedFireTruck\"><font color=\"#FF0000\">talk</font></a>) 12:12, 1 February 2021 (EST)\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Applications\">Applications</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Applications\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Application_1\">Application 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Application 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Testimonials\">Testimonials</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Testimonials\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>\"Thanks for rediscovering our theorem <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Redfiretruck&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Redfiretruck (page does not exist)\">RedFireTruck</a>\" - George and Harry of <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC50E9TuLIMWbOPUX45xZPaQ\">The Ooga Booga Tribe of The Caveman Society</a>\n</p><p>\"This is GREAT!!!\" ~ hi..\n</p><p>\"This is a very nice theorem!\" - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:RedFireTruck&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:RedFireTruck (page does not exist)\"><font color=\"#FF0000\">RedFireTruck</font></a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:RedFireTruck\" title=\"User talk:RedFireTruck\"><font color=\"#FF0000\">talk</font></a>) 10:53, 1 February 2021 (EST)\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Cooga_Georgeooga-Harryooga_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018080432\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 118/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 343/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3247/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.074      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    7.074      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20562:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018080432 and revision id 226725. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}